Target monitoring includes routing decisions, queue age, provider health, cooldown, latency, reported token/cost, failure category, gate pass rate, repair count, review findings, approval time, accepted outcome, and documentation freshness.

The platform validates and stores redacted run/eval metadata locally or at the CI evidence boundary. Credential-gated provider transports and a manual live-eval workflow can populate it, but no successful representative live record exists yet. Cost remains `null` when the provider does not expose it. No dashboard or production monitoring stack is claimed.
